    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Literature on Paradox and Circularity",
      "links": [],
      "level": 5
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Klaas Schilder: Zur Begriffsgeschichte des \"Paradoxon\". Mit besonderer Berücksichtigung Calvins und des nach-kierkegaardschen \"Paradoxon\". Kampen: J.H. Kok, 1933.\n\n\n\nPatrick Hughes and George Brecht:\nVicious Circles and Infinity. A Panoply of Paradoxes. London: Jonathan Cape, 1975.\n\n\n\nJames Cargile: Paradoxes. A study in form and predication. Cambridge, UK: Cambridge University Press, 1979.\n\n\n\n\nDouglas R. Hofstadter: Gödel, Escher, Bach. An Eternal Golden Braid. New York: Basic Books, 1979.\n\n\n\nHoward P. Kainz: Paradox, Dialectic, and System. A Contemporary Reconstruction of the Hegelian Problematic. University Park: The Pennsylvania State University Press, 1988.\n\n\n\nPeter Aczel: Non-Well-Founded Sets. CSLI\nLecture Notes, # 14. Stanford, CA: Center for the Study\nof Language and Information, 1988.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Jon Barwise and John Etchemendy.\nThe Liar: An Essay on Truth and Circularity. New York: Oxford\nUniversity Press, 1987.\n\n\n\nJon Barwise and Lawrence S. Moss: Vicious Circles. Stanford,\nCA: CSLI Publications, 1996.\n\n\n\nJ. C. Beall (ed.): Revenge of the Liar. New Essays on the Paradox. Oxford University Press, 2007.",
      "links": []
    },
